[00:18.72]1. There is a book that by its many pages,
[00:25.00]Brings peace and joy and hope to humankind.
[00:31.10]Its wondrous thoughts are charged with such great power;
[00:36.88]It brings life to the “dead,” sight to the “blind.”
[00:42.58]That precious book is God’s own Holy Bible.
[00:48.78]Its words were penned by men whom God inspired,
[00:54.88]By men who truly loved their God Jehovah,
[01:00.94]And by his holy spirit they were fired.
[01:13.06]2. They wrote a record true of God’s creations,
[01:13.34]How by his might this universe appeared.
[01:13.46]They also told how man at first was sinless
[01:42.74]But how his Paradise then disappeared.
[01:48.04]They further told about a certain angel
[01:54.14]Who challenged God and spurned his sov’reignty.
[02:00.50]That challenge led to sin and man’s great sorrow,
[02:06.64]But soon will come Jehovah’s victory.
[02:25.36]3. The time has come with reason for rejoicing:
[02:31.84]Jehovah rules by his anointed King.
[02:37.68]So now we preach the good news of the Kingdom
[02:43.64]And share the hope of blessings it will bring.
[02:49.56]Within his book are found these cheerful tidings;
[02:55.68]A sacred banquet feast on which to feed.
[03:01.98]It offers peace beyond all human thinking;
[03:08.16]This Living Treasure beckons all to read.
